From f25aed16a47f1c201c5203bb9443caf76f52cf4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <a@b.c>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:32:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: softisp: add highlight rolloff and a detail pass

The software ISP clipped highlights to white and did no detail processing,
which is most of the visible gap to the stock camera. Add two tunable knobs
to the Adjust algorithm:

- highlightKnee rolls the brightest values off instead of clipping, applied
  on the luma in the EGL shaders so the hue is kept, and in the CPU gamma
  table for the CPU debayer.
- sharpen and denoise drive a 3x3 edge-aware detail pass in the CPU debayer:
  flat areas are blended towards a local blur and edges are pushed away from
  it. The amount is chosen from the strongest channel difference so colour
  does not fringe.

Both default to off, so existing tuning files keep their old behaviour.
